SoulX-Singer (https://github.com/Soul-AILab/SoulX-Singer)
Copyright Soul AI Lab. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The singing-voice feature (`crates/local-ai/src/singing/`) runs an ONNX export of
the SoulX-Singer zero-shot singing model. The weights are **not** distributed with
this project: users download them on demand through Manager → Models
(`soulx-singer-fp16`, ~1.4 GB) under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The ONNX
graph split is the community export published on ModelScope
(`syxppp/SoulX-Singer-onnx-directml-fp16`), redistributed byte-identically.

The phoneme vocabulary `crates/local-ai/assets/phone_set.txt` (3033 tokens) is
transcribed from that model's phone set (via SXSEditor, MIT). The Mandarin
character → pinyin table `crates/local-ai/assets/zh_pinyin_map.tsv` was generated
with pinyin-pro (https://github.com/zh-lx/pinyin-pro, MIT), which itself is built
on pinyin-data (MIT).
